493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (CAN or, Controller Area Network is a differential protocol made by Bosch that is the industry standard for communication protocols over automotive solutions due to its reliability and adaptability for varying priority levels of sensors, stringent error checking capability and even a varying date size from 8 bytes to up to 64 bytes with CAN FD ! All this provides immense amounts of development options over the years, and hence why CAN is used everywhere.)
/E (CAN or, Controller Area Network is a differential protocol made by Bosch that is the industry standard for communication protocols over automotive solutions due to its reliability and adaptability for varying priority levels of sensors, stringent error checking capability and even a varying date size from 8 bytes to up to 64 bytes with CAN FD ! All this provides immense amounts of development options over the years, and hence why CAN is used everywhere.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
494 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (However this huge amount of features are restricted to hardware only, that is CAN requires a CAN controller which deciphers the information which can be used by the user as well as a CAN transceiver that is used to quantify the differential voltages in the CAN bus to something that the CAN controller can use. Also, since CAN is a communication protocol and is fast enough where reflectance has a huge impact on the amount of correct bits received, we require termination resistors \(120 ohms as specified by both MoTeC & TI\) on the CAN bus to ensure impedance matching)
/E (However this huge amount of features are restricted to hardware only, that is CAN requires a CAN controller which deciphers the information which can be used by the user as well as a CAN transceiver that is used to quantify the differential voltages in the CAN bus to something that the CAN controller can use. Also, since CAN is a communication protocol and is fast enough where reflectance has a huge impact on the amount of correct bits received, we require termination resistors \(120 ohms as specified by both MoTeC & TI\) on the CAN bus to ensure impedance matching)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Coming back to the point of the display, MoTeC is configured for using STD CAN 2.0 and the easy to use MoTeC ECU manager was used to setup the 11 bit identifier or address, along with the RPM and gear in the user defined list of sensor data to be sent over CAN, and flashing the configuration to the MoTeC ECU we start receiving information over the CAN bus with all the information with the address so that one can identify the if it is the correct sensor that they need information from. This is then followed with DLC and then 2 bytes or 4 hex digits for each channel/sensor configured, which then can be byte shifted by 8 and added up to the correct decimal value. All this information is then sent to the display via the microcontroller, and which controls the entire logic of refreshing the display.  However, this would not have been possible without the help from seniors and super-seniors and alumni that even after countless doubts asked are more than happy and excited to clear doubts when one asks for it. This is the true philosophy of Ashwa Racing since its inception )
/E (Coming back to the point of the display, MoTeC is configured for using STD CAN 2.0 and the easy to use MoTeC ECU manager was used to setup the 11 bit identifier or address, along with the RPM and gear in the user defined list of sensor data to be sent over CAN, and flashing the configuration to the MoTeC ECU we start receiving information over the CAN bus with all the information with the address so that one can identify the if it is the correct sensor that they need information from. This is then followed with DLC and then 2 bytes or 4 hex digits for each channel/sensor configured, which then can be byte shifted by 8 and added up to the correct decimal value. All this information is then sent to the display via the microcontroller, and which controls the entire logic of refreshing the display.  However, this would not have been possible without the help from seniors and super-seniors and alumni that even after countless doubts asked are more than happy and excited to clear doubts when one asks for it. This is the true philosophy of Ashwa Racing since its inception )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
